    "summary": "Cloth (woman&#039;s wrapper) narrow strips of handspun cotton, hand-woven and hand sewn together along the selvedges. The strips are of two patterns that alternate across the cloth. The first is warp-faced, with lines of red, white and indigo arranged symmetrically. The other is weft-faced, with blocks of red alternating with blocks of the same size composed of seven lines of white and indigo thread. The cloth has been hemmed by hand sewing.",
